  {
   "line": 5,
   "text": "The test wheel turns each arrow back and lays them tip to tail. On the bin, they freeze and pile up straight. Off it, the leftover arrow keeps turning, half a turn over the block, so the chain fans out: sixty-four percent. The mirror's short chain nudges it to sixty. Only whole turns close a chain.",
